From: wolfchimneyrock <12381503+wolfchimneyrock@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] MALI: bifrost: accept MEM_EXEC_INIT when the CSF EXEC_VA zone exists

CSF contexts get their EXEC_VA zone at creation (kbase_reg_zone_exec_va_init),
so KBASE_IOCTL_MEM_EXEC_INIT always returned -EPERM. libmali g29p1-11eac1
still issues it and treats -EPERM as fatal (vkCreateDevice / EGL init fail).
Accept a request that fits in the existing zone.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/arm/bifrost/mali_kbase_reg_track.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/arm/bifrost/mali_kbase_reg_track.c
@@ -1243,6 +1243,25 @@
 	 * EXEC_VA zone must come before JIT's CUSTOM_VA.
 	 */
 	if (kbase_has_exec_va_zone_locked(kctx) || kctx->jit_va) {
+#if MALI_USE_CSF
+		/* CSF contexts are created with their EXEC_VA zone already in place
+		 * (kbase_reg_zone_exec_va_init). libmali g29p1-11eac1 still asks for it
+		 * with MEM_EXEC_INIT and treats -EPERM as fatal: accept a request that
+		 * fits in the existing zone instead of refusing it.
+		 */
+		if (!kctx->jit_va) {
+			struct kbase_reg_zone *zone = kbase_ctx_reg_zone_get(kctx, EXEC_VA_ZONE);
+
+			if (exec_va_pages <= zone->va_size_pages) {
+				dev_info(kctx->kbdev->dev,
+					 "MEM_EXEC_INIT: EXEC_VA zone already set up (%llu pages), request for %llu accepted\n",
+					 (unsigned long long)zone->va_size_pages,
+					 (unsigned long long)exec_va_pages);
+				err = 0;
+				goto exit_unlock;
+			}
+		}
+#endif
 		err = -EPERM;
 		goto exit_unlock;
 	}
